This guide explains how to add the Datafy Helm repo and install the `datafy-agent`.

---

## Features
- Dual mode: sensor / autoscaler
- CSI proxy support
- Configurable env, resources, tolerations, affinity
- Pluggable token secret
- Validations (CSI presence, mode logic)
- Autogenerated values documentation (helm-docs)

---

## Installation Guide
### 1. Add Repo
```bash
helm repo add datafyio https://helm.datafy.io/datafy-agent
helm repo update
```

### 2. Install
```bash
helm install datafy-agent --version {{ template "chart.version" . }} datafyio/datafy-agent \
--namespace datafy-agent --create-namespace \
--set agent.mode="sensor/autoscaler" \
--set agent.token=<your_token> \
--atomic
```

## Upgrade
```bash
helm repo update
helm upgrade --install datafy-agent --version {{ template "chart.version" . }} datafyio/datafy-agent -n <namespace> --reuse-values --atomic
```

Switch mode:
```bash
helm upgrade --install datafy-agent --version {{ template "chart.version" . }} datafyio/datafy-agent -n <namespace> --set agent.mode=autoscaler --atomic
```

Rollback:
```bash
helm rollback datafy-agent 1 -n <namespace>
```

### 5. Verify
```bash
kubectl get pods -n <namespace> -l app.kubernetes.io/instance=datafy-agent
```
---

## Uninstall
```bash
helm uninstall datafy-agent --namespace <namespace>
```
---

## Install identity

The chart labels the controller's resources with `datafy.io/install-id` and passes the same value to the controller as `DATAFY_INSTALL_ID`. The controller only deletes resources carrying its own ID, which stops a controller left behind by a previous install from tearing down the release that replaced it.

Helm is the only writer of this value. A new ID is generated on every render — install, upgrade, or Argo CD sync — so the controller restarts on every upgrade.

## Argo CD

Argo CD renders the chart with `helm template`, so it generates a new ID every time it re-renders the chart, reports the application **OutOfSync**, and with auto-sync restarts the controller. This is safe — the labels and the controller always get the same value — but it is noise.

To keep the ID stable, pin it:

```yaml
installId: my-cluster-1
```

Change `installId` whenever the application is deleted and recreated. Reusing the old value lets a controller left behind by the previous install delete the new install's resources.

## Proxy

Set `proxy.httpsProxy` and `proxy.noProxy` to run behind an HTTPS proxy. The chart renders both the uppercase and lowercase env vars (`HTTPS_PROXY`/`https_proxy`, `NO_PROXY`/`no_proxy`) on each chart-managed container.

`noProxy` is a comma-separated list passed through verbatim. Because Helm's `--set` splits on commas, escape them or pass values via a values file.

